## 50-word bio

Lorraine K. Lee is a keynote speaker and the bestselling author of [*Unforgettable Presence*](https://amzn.to/3Hdv79r)®. She teaches on LinkedIn Learning and MasterClass, and was a founding editor at LinkedIn. She speaks at global organizations including Cisco, McKinsey, and Zoom, and has been featured in CNBC, CNN, Bloomberg, and Financial Times.

## 100-word bio

Lorraine K. Lee is an award-winning keynote speaker and the best-selling author of [*Unforgettable Presence*](https://amzn.to/3Hdv79r)®. She is also an instructor with LinkedIn Learning, Stanford, and MasterClass.

She’s on a mission to help talented leaders build an unforgettable presence — so they get recognized, get promoted, and become impossible to ignore. Lorraine has been featured in media outlets including CNBC, CNN, Forbes, Bloomberg, Fast Company, and Financial Times.

Lorraine is recognized as a LinkedIn Top Voice with hundreds of thousands of followers, and previously spent over a decade as a founding editor at companies including LinkedIn and Prezi.

## 200-word bio

Lorraine K. Lee is an award-winning keynote speaker and the bestselling author of [*Unforgettable Presence*](https://amzn.to/3Hdv79r)® — a Next Big Idea Club must-read, a #1 Amazon bestseller, and featured in Entrepreneur's Must-Read Career Books of 2025.

She’s on a mission to help talented leaders build an unforgettable presence — so they get recognized, get promoted, and become impossible to ignore. She brings that mission to Fortune 500 companies and globally recognized organizations including Zoom, Amazon, Cisco, and McKinsey & Company.

With over 300,000 LinkedIn followers and recognition as a LinkedIn Top Voice in workplace communication and presence, Lorraine’s reach extends on the stage and beyond. She teaches popular courses at MasterClass, Stanford Continuing Studies, and LinkedIn Learning, bringing her frameworks to a large global audience.

Before starting her own company, Lorraine spent over a decade as a founding editor at top tech firms including LinkedIn and Prezi, where she worked on core products including the LinkedIn Daily News module and LinkedIn Newsletters. Lorraine has been featured in media outlets including CNBC, CNN, Forbes, Bloomberg, Fast Company, and Financial Times.

She received her BSJ from Northwestern’s Medill School of Journalism and currently resides in San Francisco.
